  "notes": "West leads the ♠7 against 3NT. West's opening lead should be won by South. South has 6 top tricks (2 spades and 4 clubs). At least 2 tricks can be developed by knocking out the aces in both hearts and diamonds. If either the hearts or the diamonds break 3-3 a third trick will be available in that suit.\n\nThere is a danger that East may be able to win a heart or diamond trick and continue spades (West cannot profitably attack spades from his side of the table). If the suit that South attacks is not 3-3, the contract will likely fail.\n\nSouth can assure the contract by crossing to the dummy in clubs and leading a low heart. If East has the ♥A, he must play low or else South will have 3 heart tricks. South can win the ♥K and switch his attack to diamonds, coming to at least 9 tricks.\n\nIf West has the ♥A, the contract is still safe as a spade continuation from West will give South a third spade stopper. South will have time to develop 2 tricks in diamonds.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠7 against 3NT. West's opening lead should be won by South. South has 6 top tricks (2 spades and 4 clubs). At least 2 tricks can be developed by knocking out the aces in both hearts and diamonds. If either the hearts or the diamonds break 3-3 a third trick will be available in that suit.",
    "There is a danger that East may be able to win a heart or diamond trick and continue spades (West cannot profitably attack spades from his side of the table). If the suit that South attacks is not 3-3, the contract will likely fail.",
    "South can assure the contract by crossing to the dummy in clubs and leading a low heart. If East has the ♥A, he must play low or else South will have 3 heart tricks. South can win the ♥K and switch his attack to diamonds, coming to at least 9 tricks.",
    "If West has the ♥A, the contract is still safe as a spade continuation from West will give South a third spade stopper. South will have time to develop 2 tricks in diamonds."
